acation trips, festivals, and sunny days – and &lt;strong&gt;a way to keep a little bit of summer around for longer&lt;/strong&gt;, regardless of the weather.&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;div class="video-container"&gt;&lt;iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/9JGAtW8ib9w" width="560" height="315" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://activeshop.com.pl/media/wysiwyg/product/ocho_colors/palettes-ocho-nails-sorbet.jpg"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;h2&gt;How to properly perform a hybrid manicure?&lt;/h2&gt;  &lt;p&gt;1. Before starting the procedure, thoroughly disinfect your and the client's hands with antiseptic fluid and prepare the workplace accordingly.&lt;br&gt;2. Use a file of the appropriate gradation to give the nails the desired shape, gently mat the plate with a polishing block, and if necessary prepare the cuticles.&lt;br&gt;3. Rinse the nail plate with a cotton pad soaked in a cleanser. In addition, you can use a primer.&lt;br&gt;4. Apply a thin layer of hybrid base and cure for 30 seconds in a LED lamp or 2 minutes in a UV lamp.&lt;br&gt;5. Spread the hybrid nail polish in the selected color on the hardened base and cure for 30 sec. in the LED lamp or 2 min. in the UV lamp. You can repeat the process for more intense color.&lt;br&gt;6. Then apply a thin layer of top coat and cure for 30 sec. in an LED lamp or 2 min. in a UV lamp. Depending on the type of top, it may be necessary to wash with a cleanser.&lt;br&gt;7. We recommend applying nourishing oil to the cuticles around the nails for better care.&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://activeshop.com.pl/media/wysiwyg/product/ocho_colors/buteleczki-ocho-nails-sorbet.jpg"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
